        "original_id": "fba89e4d-5830-5bf8-a1a4-fe771c73e9c1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Modest Petrovich Mussorgsky, Arseny Golenishchev-Kutuzov\n- Works: Songs and Dances of Death\n- Roles: composer, poet\n- Organizations: The Five\n\nFacts:\n- Modest Petrovich Mussorgsky was a Russian composer who lived from 21 March 1839 to 28 March 1881.\n- Modest Petrovich Mussorgsky was one of the group known as The Five.\n- In the mid-1870s, Modest Petrovich Mussorgsky wrote Songs and Dances of Death.\n- Songs and Dances of Death is a song cycle for voice, usually bass or bass-baritone, and piano.\n- Songs and Dances of Death was written to poems by Arseny Golenishchev-Kutuzov, who was a relative of Modest Petrovich Mussorgsky.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
